## 7. Cómo comprobar el resultado

Últimos logs:

```sql
SELECT id, policy_log_id, transaction_id, preview_status, internal_note,
       push_status, transaction_push_id, updated_at
FROM push_firewall_log
ORDER BY id DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

Qué hizo cada ejecución y con qué errores:

```sql
SELECT name, created_at, finish_at, message
FROM task_date
WHERE name IN ('push_firewall_preview_checkpoint', 'push_firewall_checkpoint')
ORDER BY id DESC
LIMIT 4;
```

Políticas que entrarían en automático:

```sql
SELECT id, scheduled_time, business_day, auto, freeze, ticket
FROM push_firewall
WHERE auto = true AND freeze = false;
```

En la interfaz: **Firewall > Push Firewall > Push Firewall Logs**. Al pinchar en Log Preview o Log Push se abre el log completo con un botón para copiarlo.

Tests:

```
python manage.py test rss.test_push_firewall_checkpoint rss.test_push_firewall_preview_checkpoint
```

